<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Trikora</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1961">1961</a>–<a href="/years/1962">1962</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tri Komando Rakyat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Trikora was the Indonesian campaign of 1961–1962 to take western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, named after the 'People's Triple Command' that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukarno">Sukarno</a> proclaimed in December 1961. Indonesian forces, under a command led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suharto">Suharto</a>, landed paratroops and infiltrators while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> lost a naval clash in the Arafura Sea. Under American pressure the Netherlands signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Agreement of August 1962, and after a brief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> administration the territory passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> in 1963.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-trikora.jpg" alt="Operation Trikora" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lou Sander · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yos_Sudarso_Postage_Stamp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
